               middle temporal gyrus; and (iv) the auditory radiations-like
               component, which leaves the pulvinar accompanying the auditory
               radiations to the superomedial aspect of the temporal operculum,
               just posteriorly to Heschl's gyrus. Each of those components
               might correspond to a different level of information processing
               involved in the lexical retrieval process of picture naming.",
